In a single browser script, the following statements execute in order:

```javascript
console.log("A");
setTimeout(() => console.log("B"), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log("C"));
console.log("D");
```

Assuming no other tasks, timers, or exceptions are involved, what is the order of the four console outputs, and why?

